INSTEAD 3.6.0
=============

WARNING! For successful building you must install these development packages
(names may vary in your distribution):

	sdl3, sdl3_mixer, sdl3_image, sdl3_ttf, lua5.1/luajit, zlib, iconv

SDL3 development packages are not available in every distribution yet.
If they are missing, build and install SDL3, SDL3_ttf, SDL3_image and
SDL3_mixer from source first:
	https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL
	https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_ttf
	https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_image
	https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_mixer
The versions used by CI are listed in .github/workflows/CI.yml.

SDL3_image and SDL3_mixer use system codec libraries when they are available:
	libpng, libjpeg, libwebp, libtiff, giflib (images)
	libogg, libvorbis, opusfile, libxmp (sound, tracker music)

Optionally you may use:
	lua5.2/lua5.3/lua5.4
	HarfBuzz and SDL3_ttf compiled with HarfBuzz support

0) Prepare for building
=======================

Unpack source package with this command:
	$ tar xzvf instead_<version>.tar.gz

Change current dir to project's build dir:
	$ cd instead-<version>

There are several ways to build the package.

1) Build using cmake
====================

	$ cmake -S . -B build
	$ cmake --build build
	$ sudo cmake --install build

If cmake cannot find Lua, define LUA_INCLUDE_DIR (and LUA_LIBRARY) explicitly.
For example (Arch linux, lua5.1):
	$ cmake -S . -B build -DLUA_INCLUDE_DIR=/usr/include/lua5.1

To build standalone version, use this:
	$ cmake -S . -B build -DSTANDALONE=1
	$ cmake --build build
	$ cmake --install build
	$ cd build/standalone
	$ ./sdl-instead

Some options:
WITH_LUAJIT Use LuaJIT instead of Lua (default on)
WITH_ICONV Build with iconv support (default on)
WITH_HARFBUZZ RTL support. SDL3_ttf should be compiled with HarfBuzz too (default off)

For example, to build standalone version without LuaJIT, use:

	$ cmake -S . -B build -DWITH_LUAJIT=0 -DSTANDALONE=1

2) Build using configure.sh
===========================

	$ ./configure.sh

It checks build dependencies with pkg-config and generates config.make.
Then choose installation mode: standalone (1) or system (2).

Standalone build (runs from the source tree):
	$ make
	$ ./sdl-instead

System install:
	$ make
	$ sudo make install
	$ sdl-instead

If build process has failed check Rules.make.standalone (or Rules.make.system)
and config.make, make changes if needed.

3) Manual build
===============

To build a game that runs just from the build dir, use Rules.make.standalone:
	$ rm -f Rules.make
	$ ln -s Rules.make.standalone Rules.make
	$ make clean
	$ make
	$ ./sdl-instead

To build a game for system install, use Rules.make.system:
	$ rm -f Rules.make
	$ ln -s Rules.make.system Rules.make
	$ make clean
	$ make
	$ sudo make install
	$ sdl-instead

4) On Ubuntu
============

Install stable (older, SDL2 based) version from repo:
	$ apt-get install instead

5) On Debian based systems you can build deb package
====================================================

	$ sudo apt-get install liblua5.1-dev libsdl3-dev libsdl3-ttf-dev libsdl3-image-dev libsdl3-mixer-dev
	$ sudo apt-get install build-essential debhelper
	$ debuild
	$ cd ..
	$ sudo dpkg -i instead_<version>.deb

If SDL3 development packages are not available in your distribution, build
and install SDL3 from source first (see the top of this file).

6) On arch linux
================

Install stable version from AUR:
	$ yay -S instead

Or build from source:
	$ make PKGBUILD
	$ makepkg -s

7) On FreeBSD
=============

Install instead from ports with pkgng:
	# pkg install instead
Or:
	# cd /usr/ports/games/instead
	# make install

Or build from tarball:
	$ ./configure.sh
	$ gmake

8) On RPM based system
======================

There is .spec file in tarball.

9) Right-to-left support
========================

In order to build INSTEAD with right-to-left support, SDL3_ttf and INSTEAD
should be compiled with HarfBuzz support (see section 1 for cmake options).
SDL3_ttf has a build option TTF_USE_HARFBUZZ for it.

Enjoy.
